---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import type { Locale } from '../../i18n/ui';
import '../../styles/ai-usage.css';

const locale: Locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="AI Usage · Roomie"
	description="Disclosure of AI use across the website, the intercom development and the documentation."
	locale={locale}
>
	<header class="page-head">
		<h1>AI Usage</h1>
		<p class="page-sub">Where and how much generative AI went into roomie</p>
	</header>

	<p class="lead">
		The world is being flooded with content where no one really knows anymore what was actually
		made by human hands and what mostly comes from a generative AI. Working with generative AI is
		a real benefit for me too, but I believe that the creative process and the technical
		direction should stay in human hands. So on this page I try to lay out, in a way you can
		follow, where and to what extent I have relied on generative AI. In what follows I
		distinguish between this website, the development of the actual intercom system, and its
		documentation.
	</p>

	<section aria-labelledby="website-heading">
		<h2 id="website-heading" class="section-title">This website</h2>
		<div class="card card--mint">
			<p>
				Unless marked otherwise, the content on this website comes from me and not from an AI. The
				content of every blog post is written entirely by me, without generative AI – the one
				exception is translation between German and English, which I then revise and check by
				hand. I have noted this beneath the post in question. I also deliberately do without
				AI-assisted spelling and grammar checking – so please excuse the odd mistake&nbsp;;-)
			</p>
			<div class="split">
				<div>
					<h3>Without AI</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Idea and visual language</li>
						<li>All content and blog posts in their original version</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3>With AI support</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>
							Technical build and deployment of the website – this isn't my area of expertise, so
							I turned to Claude Code here
						</li>
						<li>
							Translations between German and English, followed by manual revision and review
						</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="intercom-heading">
		<h2 id="intercom-heading" class="section-title">Developing the intercom</h2>
		<div class="card card--sky">
			<p>
				While developing roomie I drew on ChatGPT, Claude Code and GitHub Copilot. Separating the
				contributions cleanly is hard, but it looks roughly like this:
			</p>
			<div class="split">
				<div>
					<h3>Mostly without AI</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Concept, specification and visual language</li>
						<li>System, firmware and state architecture</li>
						<li>Driver architecture</li>
						<li>Technical interfaces between the software and system modules</li>
						<li>Programming guidelines</li>
						<li>Schematic of the circuit board</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3>Mostly with AI</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>
							Fleshing out and coding individual software modules with GitHub Copilot or Claude
							Code, followed by review and manual testing – I retraced and understood almost every
							line of code by hand
						</li>
						<li>
							Producing the artwork for the "roomie mascots" – the idea of cuddly pocket monsters
							is mine; the generation was done with ChatGPT
						</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="docs-heading">
		<h2 id="docs-heading" class="section-title">Documentation</h2>
		<div class="card card--lavender">
			<p>
				The substance of the documentation is mine; since I wrote it in English, I used generative
				AI for language corrections.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<p class="ai-note">
		Notes on the use of AI for this page: the German original was written by me without generative
		AI. This English version was translated with Claude Code and then manually revised and
		checked by me.
	</p>
</BaseLayout>
